      "content": "To differentiate between localized subgrade failures and a systemic issue, you need to look closely at the cracking pattern. If the cracks are highly erratic, clustered over specific areas, or seem to correlate with known weak spots or utility trenches, then you are likely dealing with localized subgrade settlement. A widespread, uniform pattern of longitudinal cracking across the entire stretch, however, suggests a more systemic issue, possibly related to the overall mix properties or uniform thermal stresses across the entire pavement section. You might need to perform localized Falling Weight Deflectometer (FWD) tests to assess the subgrade modulus in specific zones.",
